-- title:
--   Initial-filtration conditional upper bound for original pure-jump stopped dividend reward
-- statement:
--   Prove the conditional expected upper bound for the same spectrally negative Lévy sample path with σ=0 and ¬BoundedVariation, original predictable source jumps, dividend strategy, HJB and ruin-bounded stopping clocks. The original stopped reward F has its exact discounted terminal and inclusive-Iic dividend cash formula. Conditional expectation at the right-continuous initial filtration is at most w(x) almost surely. Do this by genuine stopped Itô-Meyer on the same process, with finite-intensity negative-mark truncations, L2/L1 small-jump passage, generator sign, dividend jump/contact, and initial/ruin/horizon atoms. No W/Cash/Term auxiliary decomposition is required.
-- source:
--   Acyclic stochastic conditional source core for the UBV-JUMP11 parent c233a386. Derived independent centred witness using existing proved c80460e8 conditional expectation to witness lemma.

